[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two deep, round, matte ceramic bowls set on an aged oak wood surface with subtle wear marks. The bowls are positioned 3/4 overhead to show the rich texture of the stew, with one bowl sharp in the foreground and the second bowl softly blurred in the background. The stew is a thick, creamy, sunset-orange mixture derived from red lentils, tomatoes, and Greek yogurt, with bright, wilted streaks of dark green baby spinach folded throughout. Tiny flecks of green cilantro are scattered naturally across the surface. A wooden spoon rests casually on the table beside the main bowl, and a few stray fragments of cilantro and a tiny smear of the orange-hued sauce mark the wood surface. The lighting is soft natural side light from a window on the left, creating gentle highlights on the creamy, slightly oily sheen of the yogurt-lentil emulsion. No artificial lights or flash. The dish appears as a comforting, home-cooked meal, warm and inviting. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: a small sauce drip on the bowl rim, uneven spinach distribution, and natural steam ripples. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
  }
]
